course: dictionary
lesson: 2212
title: Same word, different meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 2
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. Coup has two. In history it means a sudden, often violent, illegal taking of power, usually by the army. In everyday talk it means a clever, successful win of something hard to get.
explain: Read the sentence, then ask which meaning fits. «In 2021 Myanmar's army took power in a coup, and a civil war followed.» The army took power illegally, so coup means a seizing of power. Swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Now look at a different use: «Getting that star player was a coup.» No army is involved, and nobody is seizing power. The clue is that a hard-to-get star player was won, so here coup means a great success. Same word, different context.
explain: Phrases give more clues. A military coup or a failed coup is about power in a country. «A real coup» in everyday talk usually praises a big win. When the context is still unclear, check a dictionary.
fact: Coup is a noun: one coup, two coups.
fact: «Coup» means a sudden, often violent, illegal taking of power in a country, usually by the army. It is also called a coup d'état.
fact: «Coup» can also mean a clever, successful action that wins something hard to get, such as a star player.
fact: «Failed coup» means an attempt to seize power that does not succeed, as in «after a failed coup» in Moscow in 1991.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so check the context before you decide which meaning fits.
exercise: «In 2021 Myanmar's army took power in a coup.» What is a coup here? | *A sudden, illegal taking of power, usually by the army | A clever win of something hard to get | A big party in the capital | A kind of weather
exercise: «Getting that star player was a real coup for the club.» What does coup mean here? | A sudden, illegal taking of power | *A clever, successful win of something hard to get | A broken window | A long journey by train
exercise: What does «failed coup» mean? | A football match that was cancelled | A coup that won an election | A plan to build a new school | *An attempt to seize power that did not succeed
test: «The army's coup shocked the whole city.» What is the best meaning of coup here? | A small argument at school | *A sudden, illegal taking of power by the army | A clever, successful win | A quiet walk in the park
test: Tom says coup always means a violent attack. What is the best reply? | Yes, but only in music shows | *Not always: it can also mean a clever, successful win of something hard to get | Yes, it always means a fight | No, it always means a holiday
exam: Find the one word in «after a failed coup» that tells you the coup did not work. | *failed | after | a | coup
